Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 02:21:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(nsmenu-spike): flag-gated AppKit NSMenu bridge (F0
 experiment)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The F0 spike from research/UI-STACK-SUCCESSOR-PRE §4: the SwiftUI
Commands main-menu family gains an AppKit twin behind the
'la.menu.nsmenuBridge' UserDefaults flag (launch line
'-la.menu.nsmenuBridge 1'; DEFAULT OFF = byte-identical face).

- NSMenuBridge.swift: one statically built NSApp.mainMenu tree,
  MenuCommandSet consumed verbatim (MenuCommandID -> NSMenuItem 1:1);
  enablement rides menuNeedsUpdate + a withObservationTracking
  adapter (no polling timer, no AttributeGraph); all action closures
  route into the app root's existing command seams (captured after
  install, the same @State-storage shape every scene-task closure
  uses) — command bodies are NOT rewritten.
- LightamerApp: the .commands block gates on !NSMenuBridge.isEnabled
  (flag ON = SwiftUI never builds its ~45 custom items — the D-6
  makeMainMenu/updateMainMenu loop fuel under test) and the wiring
  task installs the bridge after the whole state graph is wired.
- Publish-site seams (reads only): WorkspaceHostView notes the
  workspace, ContentView notes the export-panel presence,
  InspectorView notes the metadata field focus.
- DEBUG probe: '-la_probe_stay' keeps the editor probe alive after
  the rows load (AR-01 F-8 idle-probe shape for the churn driver).

Zero Core/IOP touches, zero new localization keys, zero UserDefaults
keys beyond the spike flag.
